%% title: Activation and configuration ownership
%% description: Nix configuration activates Home Manager or nix-darwin, while the convention linker handles only targets outside Home Manager ownership.
%% evidence: COMP-001, COMP-002, COMP-003, COMP-004, CTX-001
flowchart TB
  install[install] -->|Nix default path| bootstrap[nix-bootstrap]
  bootstrap -->|user activation| home_manager[Home Manager]
  bootstrap -->|system flag| darwin[nix-darwin]
  home_manager -->|owns declared shell and Git files| managed[Managed home files]
  darwin -->|reuses Home Manager module| home_manager
  linker[link-dotfiles] -->|maps convention sources| unmanaged[Unmanaged home files and public commands]
  exclusion[Home Manager target exclusion] -->|prevents duplicate ownership| linker
  work_mode[work-mode] -->|atomically writes| state[Mutable environment state]
  state -->|is sourced by| shell[Zsh startup]
